    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The runtime config matters: `petclinic.security.enable=false` and profiles `h2,spring-data-jpa` are active.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the controller runs\n\n1. **Security filter chain** \u2014 `DisableSecurityConfig` is active: CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().permitAll()`. The `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on the handler is present in source but **not enforced** (method security isn't loaded under this profile).\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** (failures \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**), field by field:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[-0-9()+.\\s]*$)`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `registrationDate` (optional): ISO date\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 `effectiveRegistrationDate(...)`\n\n3. **Default the registration date**: use supplied date, else `LocalDate.now()`.\n4. **Roll forward off weekends** to the next business day (Monday).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 `prepareNewOwner(...)` \u2014 business validation, in this exact order\n\n5. **Normalize address** (mutates the DTO in place).\n6. **`validateRequiredFields`**: firstName, lastName, **address (post-normalization)**, city, telephone must be non-blank \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (**400**).\n7. **Normalize telephone**: strip separators, force E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops leading 0), validate regex `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` and per-country national length (+61\u21929, +1\u219210); mutates DTO \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException([\"telephone\"])` (**400**).\n8. **Normalize email** (optional): validate against email pattern, store trimmed + lower-cased; mutates DTO \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException([\"email\"])` (**400**).\n9. **`validatePostcode`** (optional): 4 digits **and** within the city's regional range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException([\"postcode\"])` (**400**).\n10. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`**: builds an identity key from telephone + canonical email + prospective household id; rejects if it matches any existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**). *(reads all owners)*\n11. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`**: city (case-insensitive) must have < `CITY_OWNER_CAPACITY` (50) owners \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (**409**). *(reads all owners)*\n12. **`rejectDailyLimitExceeded`**: < `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT` (100) owners for that registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**). *(reads all owners)*\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Build the entity & derived fields\n\n13. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via MapStruct (`id` and `pets` ignored).\n14. **Set `registrationDate`** (the business-day-adjusted value).\n15. **Set `customerCode`** = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, sequence = existing count in that city + 1. *(reads all owners)*\n16. **Set `namesakeCount`** = count of existing owners with same first+last, case-insensitive. *(reads all owners)*\n17. **`assignHousehold`** (when `sharesHousehold == true`): compute `HH-<sha256 prefix>` from lastName + normalized address; set it on the new owner **and update every existing household mate** \u2014 extra `saveOwner` writes to other rows (side effect on other records). *(reads all owners)*\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Persist\n\n18. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional`; Spring Data `save` \u2192 `persist` (id is null). Note: `addOwner` itself is **not** `@Transactional`, so every count/read above and this write run in separate transactions. Hibernate/entity-level constraints (e.g. `@NotEmpty`, telephone `@Pattern` on the entity) are checked at flush.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 After persist\n\n19. **Set transient `householdMemberCount`** = count of members in the owner's household. *(reads all owners)*\n20. **Audit log**: `AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...\")`.\n21. **Map `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`**, computing derived fields (displayName, initials, membershipNumber, `membershipLevel` [base 1, +1 if email, +1 if namesakeCount==0, cap 3], `contactPreference` [EMAIL if email else PHONE], locality, etc.).\n22. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** on the response DTO if that day's signups exceed `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (80).\n23. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Cross-cutting\n\n- **`@ControllerAdvice` (`ExceptionControllerAdvice`)** converts each exception above into a `ProblemDetail` with the noted status codes.\n- **No** `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist` callbacks, **no** `ApplicationEventPublisher` events, and **no** password encoding exist on this path.\n\nThe most notable non-obvious behaviors: the endpoint **silently mutates the input** (address/telephone/email normalization, weekend\u2192Monday date rolling), makes **many separate full-table reads** of all owners across independent transactions, and **writes to other owners' rows** when household sharing is enabled."
  },
